# Server scripts run on FreeBSD (MyDevil) — never check them out with CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
# The 10x CLI hashes its managed block in CLAUDE.md byte for byte; a CRLF checkout makes it
# look locally modified and the CLI skips every later lesson's rules.
CLAUDE.md text eol=lf
# Same for every other file the 10x CLI writes and tracks by hash (prompts, config templates,
# the .agents skill): a CRLF checkout turns each one into a "skipped-conflict" on `10x sync`.
.claude/prompts/** text eol=lf
.claude/config-templates/** text eol=lf
.agents/skills/** text eol=lf
